# Files that VSeerr maintains itself. When a Seerr release is merged into
# VSeerr, these paths always keep VSeerr's version, so upstream edits to them
# never cause conflicts. Read by .github/workflows/vseerr-upstream-check.yml.
# Check the release notes for anything worth copying over by hand.
# One path per line; lines starting with # are ignored.
.github/README.md
.github/CODEOWNERS
.github/PULL_REQUEST_TEMPLATE.md
.github/ISSUE_TEMPLATE/config.yml
.github/renovate.json5
vseerr-docs/
CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md
CONTRIBUTING.md
NOTICE.md
SECURITY.md
